WEBVTT

00:01.930 --> 00:05.720
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.220
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.570 --> 00:15.410
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.410 --> 00:20.690
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.690 --> 00:25.340
<i><i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:26.820 --> 00:30.920
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.920 --> 00:34.100
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.630
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.330 --> 02:14.460
<b>A Trash Game Realignment of Elevated Tastes</b>

02:27.140 --> 02:28.620
Heading to the dojo?

02:28.620 --> 02:30.330
Y-Yes!

02:30.550 --> 02:32.180
Um, well...

02:32.180 --> 02:36.430
I thought I'd see if you had any 
good games before practice...

02:36.430 --> 02:38.410
Hizutome-kun's not here, just so you know.

02:39.370 --> 02:41.420
Um, I...

02:41.420 --> 02:45.500
It's summer break, so he's probably 
been immersed this whole time...

02:44.050 --> 02:46.520
<b>Summer Break Promotion!!
Now Adding Servers!</b>

02:47.010 --> 02:48.730
You still haven't found him?

02:51.230 --> 02:55.720
Well, you said he always plays as "Sunraku,"

02:55.720 --> 02:58.620
so I've been looking for 
him under that name...

02:58.960 --> 03:03.490
But he seems to have skipped the 
first tutorial city entirely...

03:06.260 --> 03:08.510
He's charting his own course, huh?

03:08.510 --> 03:10.710
Typical trash game fanatic.

03:11.030 --> 03:13.570
He'll do things normal players won't do,

03:13.570 --> 03:16.760
and run into all kinds of 
outrageous unique scenarios!

03:16.760 --> 03:19.080
But as the first thing he does in the game?

03:20.720 --> 03:23.670
Well... I guess it does seem plausible.

03:23.670 --> 03:26.360
I'm sure you'll find him soon.

03:26.360 --> 03:28.470
Keep going, Rei-chan!

03:29.130 --> 03:30.330
Okay...

03:30.330 --> 03:32.010
Then tell him how you feel.

03:37.860 --> 03:39.670
I'm heading out!

03:39.670 --> 03:40.900
Sure.

03:41.170 --> 03:44.260
I've got work after, so I'll be out late!

03:41.950 --> 03:45.070
<b>Rumi Hizutome</b>

03:44.860 --> 03:46.610
Sure.

03:49.570 --> 03:54.070
"Unique scenarios recommended for beginners."

03:55.020 --> 03:58.220
"Tour of Rabituza" trigger conditions...

03:58.590 --> 04:00.800
<b>Shangri-La Frontier Guide</b>

03:58.590 --> 04:00.800
<b>Tour of Rabituza</b>

03:58.810 --> 03:59.850
That must be this.

04:02.310 --> 04:08.280
"If you defeat a monster of higher level 
than you with Vorpal weapons equipped,

04:08.280 --> 04:14.270
a special Vorpal Bunny will appear in 
any town and invite you to Rabituza."

04:17.400 --> 04:21.040
"The Vorpal Bunny will just keep 
running without saying anything,

04:21.040 --> 04:23.280
so make sure you don't lose sight of it."

04:23.510 --> 04:27.150
"Once you arrive, if you 
defeat the Lagonian Python,

04:27.150 --> 04:29.400
a monster terrorizing their city,

04:29.400 --> 04:33.290
you'll learn the 'Enchant Vorpal' spell."

04:33.620 --> 04:38.490
Yeah, that's nothing like the unique 
scenario I played yesterday.

04:38.990 --> 04:41.800
That sure wasn't a Python I encountered.

04:42.420 --> 04:48.680
It was an intimidating—if not as much 
as Lycagon—yakuza boss-looking bunny.

04:49.290 --> 04:50.260
Well?

04:50.880 --> 04:54.440
Mind giving me a bit of your time?

04:55.400 --> 04:57.940
I'm the boss here in Rabituza.

04:57.940 --> 04:59.570
The name's Vysache.

05:00.270 --> 05:04.400
You gave that pup quite a fight, didn't you?

05:09.170 --> 05:12.200
That's a hell of a vorpal soul you've got.

05:16.310 --> 05:19.010
What in the world is a "vorpal soul"?

05:24.470 --> 05:25.370
What do you think?

05:25.820 --> 05:30.550
I'd be happy to get you up to 
snuff, if you're up for it.

05:31.000 --> 05:32.190
Get me up to snuff?

05:33.930 --> 05:35.680
<i>Oh, I get it now!</i>

05:36.330 --> 05:38.360
<i>It's a training quest!</i>

05:39.000 --> 05:43.030
<i>Unique scenario training could 
yield unprecedented buffs!</i>

05:43.800 --> 05:44.990
<i>I have no reason to refuse!</i>

05:46.620 --> 05:48.240
I place myself in your hands...

05:48.880 --> 05:49.760
Aniki.

05:54.570 --> 05:56.010
"Aniki"?

06:03.550 --> 06:06.800
O-Oh, that was just a little joke...

06:07.800 --> 06:10.390
Oh, crap!

06:10.820 --> 06:14.140
Did I choose the wrong response?!

06:20.870 --> 06:23.060
Hey, I like you.

06:23.060 --> 06:26.780
Asking for my training <i>does</i>
make you my underling!

06:27.150 --> 06:29.070
Glad you know how these things work.

06:29.470 --> 06:31.790
Feel free to call me Vash.

06:32.260 --> 06:34.790
That's a privilege I afford 
to people with potential.

06:35.580 --> 06:39.280
'K-'Kay... Aniki Vash.

06:40.580 --> 06:42.420
<i>I'm so glad it was the right choice!</i>

06:42.420 --> 06:44.920
<i>I thought he was gonna skin me alive!</i>

06:44.920 --> 06:45.800
Emul!

06:45.800 --> 06:47.080
Yes?!

06:47.080 --> 06:48.760
Dadd— I mean, Boss?!

06:49.150 --> 06:52.260
I'm putting him in your care.

06:54.180 --> 06:54.980
Yes!

06:54.980 --> 06:57.290
I'm going to work <i>so</i> hard!

06:57.290 --> 06:59.140
So, <i>so</i> hard!

06:59.140 --> 07:02.020
So, so, <i>so</i> hard!

07:04.020 --> 07:05.510
All right, Sunraku-san!

07:05.510 --> 07:07.860
Allow me to give you a tour of the palace!

07:07.860 --> 07:09.630
H-Hang on a minute!

07:09.630 --> 07:12.470
It's been a pretty long play session for me.

07:12.470 --> 07:14.490
I was thinking of taking a break.

07:15.180 --> 07:18.000
Oh, really? That's a shame...

07:18.500 --> 07:22.870
<i>And I'd like to look up more about 
unique scenarios and unique monsters.</i>

07:22.870 --> 07:25.840
I'll show you to one of our inns, then!

07:25.840 --> 07:26.920
Oh, really?

07:26.920 --> 07:29.200
I can register my respawn point here?

07:27.520 --> 07:30.260
* Respawn Point:
A location from which you can resume play.

07:29.200 --> 07:30.260
Sounds great!

07:30.620 --> 07:32.640
Leave every little thing to me!

07:35.050 --> 07:38.020
Oh, right. I forgot about this.

07:42.140 --> 07:44.070
Wh-What the heck?

07:44.070 --> 07:45.710
A forced equip item?

07:46.570 --> 07:49.490
<b>Vorpal Soul Collar
</b>acquired.

07:47.140 --> 07:49.610
"Vorpal Soul Collar" acquired.

07:49.840 --> 07:51.110
While equipped, user receives half EXP
but gains 2.5x stat points
(rounded down) when leveling.

07:52.030 --> 07:54.460
It halves the EXP I receive?!

07:54.460 --> 07:55.240
Hang on!

07:55.240 --> 07:56.240
It's no use.

07:57.310 --> 08:00.540
You can't take that off unless I allow it.

08:01.140 --> 08:06.540
Extraordinary hardship is necessary 
for the weak to grow stronger.

08:06.840 --> 08:10.020
Never forget the vorpal soul.

08:10.420 --> 08:12.970
It suits you very well, Sunraku-san!

08:13.450 --> 08:14.340
I...

08:14.860 --> 08:20.100
I've been saddled with another restriction?!

08:21.630 --> 08:23.850
Two point five times stat points, huh?

08:24.240 --> 08:28.770
Even if it does halve my EXP received, 
that's a pretty big upside.

08:29.110 --> 08:31.360
Kind of broken, to say the least.

08:32.640 --> 08:36.730
No one on the forums seems to 
know about Vysache or Emul,

08:36.730 --> 08:39.420
let alone the Vorpal Soul Collar.

08:39.850 --> 08:44.040
No one's found a unique scenario where 
you enter the Palace of Rabituza.

08:44.790 --> 08:48.270
A unique scenario only I know about!

08:48.270 --> 08:49.680
That's pretty exciting!

08:51.120 --> 08:53.110
Whoops, time for my appointment.

08:57.730 --> 09:01.470
Stupid Katzo. 
Why'd we have to do this in <i>BERP</i>?

09:02.120 --> 09:03.730
I haven't logged into this game in forever.

09:04.300 --> 09:06.410
<i><i>Berserk Online Passion</i>.</i>

09:06.410 --> 09:08.120
<i><i>BOP</i> for short.</i>

09:06.410 --> 09:09.230
<b>BOP → BERP</b>

09:08.120 --> 09:09.230
<i>Or, derisively, <i>BERP</i>.</i>

09:14.370 --> 09:18.580
<i><i>BERP</i> is a fighting game 
Rakuro once got deeply into.</i>

09:18.580 --> 09:20.910
<i>It is, naturally, a trash game.</i>

09:22.250 --> 09:26.560
<i>Its playerbase has waned to less 
than a hundred sign-ins per day,</i>

09:26.560 --> 09:29.350
<i>leaving many to wonder why 
the service is still running.</i>

09:29.350 --> 09:34.800
<i>Which means most of those 
who remain know each other,</i>

09:34.650 --> 09:36.510
<b>Sunraku</b>

09:34.800 --> 09:37.020
<i>and are of a single kind—</i>

09:37.390 --> 09:39.180
<i>trash game enthusiasts.</i>

09:38.820 --> 09:40.280
<b>Modor Katzo</b>

09:42.010 --> 09:44.000
You've shown yourself at last, Sunraku.

09:44.000 --> 09:45.450
Shall we get right to it?

09:49.730 --> 09:50.680
What are the rules?

09:53.610 --> 09:55.280
<i>Ready? Fight!</i>

09:56.000 --> 09:57.990
You know what they are...

09:58.340 --> 09:59.790
Vale tudo!

09:58.510 --> 10:01.490
<b>* Vale tudo = "Anything goes" in Portuguese</b>

09:59.790 --> 10:02.010
"Anything goes"!

10:03.270 --> 10:05.750
That's some creepy-ass glitching.

10:05.750 --> 10:10.380
It's a new move I worked out 
while you were focused on <i>Failia</i>!

10:10.380 --> 10:13.310
NSFW Tentacle Attack!

10:13.310 --> 10:16.430
You developed a new glitch, huh?

10:16.430 --> 10:19.870
How'd a madman like you 
get to be a pro gamer?

10:19.870 --> 10:21.090
Modor Katzo...

10:22.830 --> 10:24.260
Quick-Draw Fist!

10:24.590 --> 10:25.310
What?!

10:31.240 --> 10:33.880
I'm using a delay, 
but he's still blocking them?!

10:33.880 --> 10:36.400
You're the madman, 
with reaction speed like that!

10:36.400 --> 10:39.480
Quick-Draw Fist is the ultimate style!

10:39.480 --> 10:41.430
Theoretically, as long as 
you've got twelve frames,

10:41.430 --> 10:43.910
you can even counter boss 
insta-kill attacks unscathed!

10:43.910 --> 10:46.660
I'll break through all your hits!

10:50.640 --> 10:51.260
Huh?

10:51.260 --> 10:53.070
Hey, Modor Katzo's fighting!

10:54.080 --> 10:56.430
Hey! Isn't that Sunraku?!

10:56.430 --> 10:57.510
Really?

10:57.510 --> 10:59.410
<i>Though this is considered a trash game,</i>

10:57.510 --> 11:00.070
That's a top-tier match-up!

10:59.410 --> 11:01.800
<i>the reason for its niche 
appeal is on display here.</i>

11:02.100 --> 11:05.360
<i>Vale tudo—Rather, "Bug tudo"—</i>

11:05.360 --> 11:06.810
<i>"Any bug goes."</i>

11:13.150 --> 11:14.400
Heck yeah!

11:16.200 --> 11:20.400
The afterimage fist textures 
were part of the hitbox?!

11:20.650 --> 11:21.910
<i>You lose!</i>

11:23.190 --> 11:27.490
Still, I've only been fighting NPCs lately.

11:27.490 --> 11:30.940
Getting a PvP trashgamium recharge 
really hit the spot, Katzo.

11:31.520 --> 11:34.920
When you emailed me to say 
you were taking on <i>SLF</i>,

11:34.920 --> 11:38.080
I figured it was a bad joke. So it was true?

11:38.080 --> 11:41.680
I'm not ashamed to say, 
I'm pretty darn into it!

11:43.260 --> 11:45.180
I guess I'll see pigs flying tomorrow.

11:45.510 --> 11:46.770
Hear me out.

11:47.210 --> 11:49.180
I've been reading the forums.

11:49.180 --> 11:54.510
<i>SLF</i>'s got these crazy strong 
monsters called the Seven Colossi.

11:49.770 --> 11:54.940
<b>The Seven Colossi</b>

11:55.150 --> 11:59.770
The playerbase has only managed to 
even get the names of four of them.

12:00.130 --> 12:01.190
So?

12:01.190 --> 12:05.820
No one's beaten a single one of 
them since the service started.

12:07.690 --> 12:09.200
Aw, it's over already?

12:09.200 --> 12:10.890
Darn! I missed it!

12:10.890 --> 12:12.020
Hey, that's Sunraku!

12:12.020 --> 12:13.500
It was awesome, man!

12:13.810 --> 12:15.930
A raging battle of bugs!

12:13.810 --> 12:16.920
So I fought one of them...

12:22.240 --> 12:24.240
And it wasted me.

12:26.520 --> 12:28.560
So that's why you're so into it?

12:28.990 --> 12:32.930
At least, I doubt I'll set it 
down until I beat that mutt.

12:36.850 --> 12:39.750
Maybe I'll start playing <i>SLF</i>, too.

12:40.630 --> 12:41.580
For real?!

12:41.580 --> 12:45.190
Hearing you talk it up piques my interest.

12:45.190 --> 12:48.950
Besides, none of my IRL friends play <i>BERP</i>.

12:50.640 --> 12:51.960
Oh, right!

12:51.960 --> 12:54.000
You-know-who is playing <i>SLF</i>, too.

12:54.260 --> 12:55.750
"You-know-who"?

12:55.750 --> 12:59.500
I sent 'em an email that 
you were playing, too.

12:59.500 --> 13:01.380
Since it's such a big deal.

13:08.510 --> 13:12.020
<b>Sunraku's Picked Up <i>SLF</i></b>

13:08.510 --> 13:12.020
From: Modor Katzo
 to: Me

13:08.510 --> 13:12.020
I hear Sunraku bought SLF.
He's pretty into it too.
Watch out for signs of hell freezing over.
TBF, I've been curious about it, too.
If he's playing it, it might be worth trying...

13:08.970 --> 13:12.020
"Sunraku's Picked Up <i>SLF</i>"?

13:12.500 --> 13:15.960
That trash game addict, playing <i>SLF</i>?

13:18.270 --> 13:20.580
I always thought he had some condition

13:21.210 --> 13:23.780
where he'd die if he ever 
stopped playing trash games.

13:40.170 --> 13:42.670
<b><i>Arthur Pencilgon</i></b>

13:46.650 --> 13:51.300
I'll have to oh-so-gently 
guide him through it.

13:59.690 --> 14:03.200
<b>Secondale - Back Alley</b>

14:03.210 --> 14:05.550
Hey, we're really back!

14:05.550 --> 14:07.450
It's called a teleport gate.

14:07.890 --> 14:11.790
A trivial matter for me, of course!

14:11.790 --> 14:13.760
<i>Emul's a handy little thing.</i>

14:13.760 --> 14:17.710
And... maybe it comes from 
playing <i>BERP</i> for a while,

14:17.710 --> 14:21.010
but these <i>SLF</i> avatars are 
easy as hell to move in!

14:21.760 --> 14:25.300
But the minute you woke up, 
you wanted to go elsewhere.

14:25.300 --> 14:26.430
Why?

14:26.900 --> 14:29.590
There's lots of fun places 
in the Palace of Rabituza!

14:29.590 --> 14:32.260
An arena, a training hall, and more!

14:32.260 --> 14:34.840
Oh, I'm totally interested in the palace, too,

14:34.840 --> 14:37.030
and I really want a good tour of it.

14:37.030 --> 14:41.190
But I'd really like to get to Thirdrema 
before the crowds start pouring in.

14:41.190 --> 14:43.020
Crowds?

14:47.770 --> 14:52.120
There's been a big uptick in players 
since summer break started, right?

14:52.430 --> 14:55.160
The forums report that the 
starter town, Firstia,

14:55.160 --> 14:57.510
is packed to the gills with new players.

14:57.510 --> 14:59.870
This city won't be far behind.

14:59.870 --> 15:01.290
Ah, yes, indeed!

15:01.290 --> 15:05.060
Which means we're gonna 
see logjams at facilities,

15:05.060 --> 15:07.690
and fights over monsters and mining spots.

15:07.690 --> 15:09.260
Ah, yes, indeed!

15:09.260 --> 15:12.760
I hear Thirdrema is a pretty big city.

15:12.760 --> 15:16.570
If I'm gonna whole-ass that unique scenario,

15:16.570 --> 15:20.230
I'd like to do it from a big city 
with plenty of breathing room.

15:20.230 --> 15:22.160
Ah, yes, indeed!

15:23.070 --> 15:24.110
You're following all this?

15:24.110 --> 15:26.480
I don't actually know 
what most of that means!

15:26.480 --> 15:27.800
Okay, so you weren't.

15:28.250 --> 15:32.300
But if you wish to reach the next city, 
I'll gladly help you get there!

15:32.880 --> 15:33.870
You've received a party request
from NPC "Magical Bunny Emul."
Accept?

15:32.970 --> 15:33.870
No

15:32.970 --> 15:33.870
Yes

15:33.870 --> 15:35.590
A party request?

15:33.870 --> 15:37.450
You've received a party request
from NPC "Magical Bunny Emul."
Accept?

15:33.870 --> 15:37.450
No

15:33.870 --> 15:37.450
Yes

15:35.590 --> 15:37.410
I can have NPCs in my party?

15:38.710 --> 15:42.210
Well, you can't reach Rabituza 
or the palace without me!

15:42.430 --> 15:46.270
I get that, but I figured 
you'd just tag along...

15:46.960 --> 15:47.460
You've received a party request
from NPC "Magical Bunny Emul."
Accept?

15:46.960 --> 15:47.460
No

15:46.960 --> 15:47.460
Yes

15:47.520 --> 15:49.090
NPC "Magical Bunny Emul"
has joined your party.

15:50.110 --> 15:52.050
<b><i>Emul</i></b>

15:50.110 --> 15:52.050
<b>Sorcerer</b>

15:50.110 --> 15:52.050
Vorpal Bunny Traveler

15:50.110 --> 15:52.050
Skill Points Remaining: 0

15:50.110 --> 15:52.050
Cash on Hand:                                   0 Mahni

15:53.350 --> 15:56.100
<i>She's mostly got better stats than me.</i>

15:56.100 --> 15:59.160
<i>Speed's the only place where 
I've got a slight edge.</i>

15:59.160 --> 16:02.190
<i>No problem. Just overtake her soon enough.</i>

16:02.190 --> 16:02.870
<i>Right.</i>

16:04.230 --> 16:10.030
<i>I'm pretty sure Lycagon's Mark is the 
trigger for that unique scenario...</i>

16:10.490 --> 16:14.820
<i>I wonder if Emul is the game's 
way of making up for it.</i>

16:14.820 --> 16:16.770
<i>If so, it's good design.</i>

16:17.240 --> 16:19.000
Let's work together, Emul.

16:19.000 --> 16:20.060
Okay!

16:20.060 --> 16:21.970
Let's work together, Sunraku-san!

16:29.190 --> 16:30.400
So cute!

16:30.400 --> 16:32.320
Where'd you get that rabbit?!

16:32.320 --> 16:34.000
Is that a Vorpal Bunny?

16:34.000 --> 16:35.520
Can you take them as pets?

16:35.520 --> 16:38.350
And did I just see it talk?!

16:38.350 --> 16:40.090
Wait, a bird?

16:40.090 --> 16:41.920
Half-naked?! Pervert?!

16:41.920 --> 16:44.190
You're a very excitable person!

16:44.430 --> 16:46.430
Yes! It talked!

16:44.430 --> 16:47.690
<i>Crap... we've been talking this whole 
time so I stopped thinking about it,</i>

16:46.430 --> 16:48.170
Hey, hey! What's your name?

16:47.690 --> 16:51.160
<i>but Emul's an NPC attached to a 
never-before-seen unique scenario!</i>

16:48.170 --> 16:49.510
I'm Emul!

16:49.510 --> 16:50.950
Emul-chan!

16:50.950 --> 16:54.200
Hey, Emul-chan, how can 
I get you in my party?

16:51.160 --> 16:53.570
<i>Since I've got it to myself for now,</i>

16:53.570 --> 16:56.310
<i>I'd like to keep it a secret 
until I can clear it...</i>

16:54.800 --> 16:56.310
Well, you can—

16:56.310 --> 16:58.700
Zip that lip!

16:59.690 --> 17:02.690
That was my ventriloquism act!

17:02.690 --> 17:05.150
Heavens, I must be off!

17:04.240 --> 17:05.580
Wait!

17:06.380 --> 17:10.590
Aw, I wanted to know how you tame them!

17:11.570 --> 17:16.050
File Saved

17:12.610 --> 17:16.050
I got a screenshot!
Let's ask on the forums!

17:23.230 --> 17:24.350
Great.

17:24.350 --> 17:26.810
There aren't any more players
nearby now, at least.

17:27.870 --> 17:30.770
I'm terribly ill-suited to 
all this running around!

17:30.770 --> 17:33.660
What kind of rabbit says a thing like that?

17:33.660 --> 17:36.610
Besides, you've got about 
the same speed stat as I do.

17:36.850 --> 17:39.740
Now, what would you have us do next?

17:40.000 --> 17:41.430
Good question.

17:41.430 --> 17:43.780
Actually, there's something I wanna confirm.

17:43.780 --> 17:45.250
Confirm?

17:45.560 --> 17:48.500
There's that line in my curse... the mark.

17:48.920 --> 17:55.630
"Monsters of lower level than the 
afflicted character will flee."

18:14.170 --> 18:16.180
It fled from you, Sunraku-san!

18:16.180 --> 18:18.910
Like it spotted some kind of degenerate.

18:19.310 --> 18:20.910
Okay, perfect!

18:22.810 --> 18:24.650
First, I chase at top speed!

18:25.290 --> 18:27.210
I don't just pursue mindlessly,

18:27.210 --> 18:30.420
but chase it into an obstacle!

18:31.220 --> 18:32.420
And then...

18:32.670 --> 18:35.170
the moment it changes direction,

18:35.450 --> 18:36.260
I throw!

18:38.780 --> 18:40.770
Then, once it's stopped,

18:41.140 --> 18:44.940
I strike at the fastest speed I can muster!

18:46.780 --> 18:48.980
An attack bonus from inertia...

18:49.420 --> 18:52.150
It's a law of physics you take 
for granted in the real world,

18:52.150 --> 18:55.290
but very few games actually 
try to replicate it.

18:56.030 --> 19:01.620
Naturally, this game models 
reality as close as it can!

19:01.620 --> 19:03.900
That was spectacular, Sunraku-san!

19:03.900 --> 19:06.790
I could hardly tell which 
one was the monster!

19:06.790 --> 19:08.300
Was that supposed to be a compliment?

19:11.310 --> 19:12.250
Okay!

19:12.250 --> 19:16.460
Even with the mark, I know I can take 
out monsters that speed or slower.

19:16.890 --> 19:18.080
I've verified what I needed to,

19:18.080 --> 19:20.230
so here's the plan!

19:22.370 --> 19:23.970
Ignore the scrubs!

19:23.970 --> 19:25.840
Straight to the area boss!

19:25.840 --> 19:26.940
That is all!

19:26.940 --> 19:29.480
That wasn't much of a plan!

19:29.810 --> 19:31.170
Now, as befits us speedsters,

19:31.170 --> 19:32.570
let's get there speedily!

19:32.570 --> 19:33.350
Away we go!

19:33.350 --> 19:36.350
To the area boss, and Thirdrema beyond!

19:36.350 --> 19:38.480
Yeah!

19:39.130 --> 19:40.860
Um...

19:40.860 --> 19:46.200
According to the map, the area 
boss is around here, but...

19:47.530 --> 19:49.590
It's swamp as far as the eye can see.

19:52.360 --> 19:55.530
This will simply <i>ruin</i> my clothing...

19:55.530 --> 19:58.680
<i>Yeah, no, I think I get it.</i>

19:58.680 --> 20:01.260
<i>With what Emul said on 
the way here and all...</i>

20:01.930 --> 20:04.450
I was in such a hurry to get out of town,

20:04.450 --> 20:06.980
I never got a chance to ask about the boss.

20:06.980 --> 20:08.670
You know anything about it, Emul?

20:08.990 --> 20:12.410
Well, it's a monster named Mud Digger!

20:12.410 --> 20:15.500
It rockets out of the ground to attack,

20:15.500 --> 20:18.400
so it's crucial to find a 
way to hold it in place!

20:18.780 --> 20:20.290
<i>"Mud Digger"...</i>

20:20.290 --> 20:22.330
<i>I gotta fight it in the swamp.</i>

20:22.710 --> 20:24.610
<i>I might be in trouble here.</i>

20:26.460 --> 20:28.250
Sunraku-san, it's here!

20:32.180 --> 20:33.150
Get on my shoulder!

20:33.540 --> 20:34.830
Righty-o!

20:49.580 --> 20:53.060
<i>A characteristic of </i>Shangri-La 
Frontier<i>'s "swamp" terrain</i>

20:54.480 --> 20:57.640
<i>is that it forces a "walking state."</i>

20:57.640 --> 21:01.020
<i>One leg always remains trapped in the marsh</i>

21:01.020 --> 21:03.130
<i>until the other foot reaches the bottom.</i>

21:05.530 --> 21:07.870
<b>Mud Digger</b>

21:05.530 --> 21:07.870
<b>Area Boss</b>

21:05.530 --> 21:07.870
Rec. Party Size: 4

21:06.480 --> 21:07.470
<i>In other words...</i>

21:08.960 --> 21:12.940
<i>This is my worst match-up possible!</i>

22:43.920 --> 22:51.180
<b>SLF Mini</b>

22:44.620 --> 22:48.440
<i><i>SLF</i></i> Theater!

22:48.440 --> 22:49.980
Mini!

22:51.430 --> 22:53.290
Okay, I'm gonna get some sleep.

22:53.290 --> 22:54.900
Night!

22:55.700 --> 22:57.440
Logged Out

22:57.440 --> 23:01.360
Sunraku-san, have a nice rest!

23:02.090 --> 23:05.440
I'll take a break, too, then.

23:17.440 --> 23:22.820
I feel so much better in my true form!

23:22.820 --> 23:26.650
Sunraku-san...

23:26.650 --> 23:30.840
Good night, now!

23:36.980 --> 23:37.900
A dream?

23:41.410 --> 23:46.920
<b>In fact, when players are logged out,
their avatars disappear.</b>
